        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-08T11:32:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that\u0027s fine, I wonder in the future if we would want to share virtual power domains. I guess in that case we have to keep those on list and loop over in `pkvm_device_pm_toggle`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 216,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 216,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "2df90823aedb72e1e7c5a42b5441d27e8804316e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b3d5a3a6_f2bb9b48",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/coco/pkvm-guest/arm-pkvm-guest.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 216,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-09T14:07:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the only reason to share the virtual power domain would be to save N HVCs per off/on where the power domain is shared by N + 1 devices. \n\nWe can look into it if there are some performance issues, but compared to the added complexity for crosvm and pvmfw (and this driver) I\u0027m not convinced this is worth supporting now.",
      "parentUuid": "c2ebf607_7ab1754a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 216,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 216,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "2df90823aedb72e1e7c5a42b5441d27e8804316e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
