    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46e7663b_87fc5cef",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/coco/pkvm-guest/arm-pkvm-guest.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 216,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-17T13:13:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, my main worry was that if multiple (physical) devices share a single pPD, allowing them to be in separate vPDs leads to a hypervisor API that\u0027s very awkward to implement as - with out current semantics - `HVC(KVM_DEV_REQ_PWR)` on one device would have to hang until it\u0027s called on all the others due to the conflicting requirements of:\n\n- vPDs not being allowed to change states unless the guest requested it\n- `HVC(KVM_DEV_REQ_PWR)` having to be synchronous (at least for \"on\")\n\n\u003e performance issues, but [...] I\u0027m not convinced this is worth supporting now.\n\nI agree that optimizing toggling devices (from separate pPDs) within a unified vPD is out of scope.",
      "parentUuid": "e423dd47_1ccce9b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 216,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 216,
        "endChar": 58
